  "sourceTitle": "Marinated Spareribs",
  "sourceText": "Marinated Spareribs\nBy: Anonymous\nPublished: Saturday, December 12, 2009 - 11:38pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n6 pounds Baby back ribs\n4 Cloves garlic, chopped\n1/4 cup Cider vinegar\n6 ounces Pineapple juice\n2 tablespoons Brown sugar\n2 tablespoons Soy sauce\n1/4 cup Brown sugar\n2 tablespoons Paprika\nChile powder\n2 teaspoons Salt\n2 teaspoons Dry mustard\n2 Bay leaves\n1/2 teaspoon Chili powder\n1/4 teaspoon Cayenne pepper\n1/4 cup Worcestershire sauce\n1 Lime juice\n2 cups Orange juice\n1/2 cup Catsup\n1 cup Water\n2 Cloves garlic, chopped\n1 Onion, chopped fine\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Marinate ribs overnight. Steam for 1 hour before grilling. 2 Mix all sauce ingredients in large saucepan. Bring to boil over high heat. 3 Simmer until slightly thickened, about 30 minutes. Discard bay leaves.",
